# Copy to .env for machine-local overrides. Loading order per project:
#   .env.base -> .env (solution root) -> <project>/.env.base -> <project>/.env
# Later files win. Comments must sit on their own line — inline comments parse
# differently across tools. `just signals init` fills the signals part for you.

# PostgreSQL. The default is the container `just db up` starts on 5473.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://suwinvtools:suwinvtools@localhost:5473/suwinvtools

# Where ticker snapshots and EDGAR documents are cached (default: <solution root>/.artifacts/market).
# SUWINVTOOLS_MARKET_CACHE=/var/cache/suwinvtools-market

# SEC EDGAR asks automated callers to identify themselves; requests without a User-Agent
# are refused. Your own "name email".
# SEC_USER_AGENT=Your Name your@email.example

# Tickers EDGAR has no ticker on record for (several ADRs). Format: TICKER:CIK, comma
# separated. Without an entry the symbol simply falls back to the provider's shorter history.
# SEC_CIK_OVERRIDES=SE:1703399

# --- signals (the monthly AI cycle job) ---
# Discord webhooks: green (mute it on Discord if you like), red, and status (INVALID readings,
# unconfirmed claims, the run summary). Empty = that channel is off.
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_GREEN=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/<id>/<token>
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_RED=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/<id>/<token>
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_STATUS=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/<id>/<token>
# Mentioned in every red message so it pings on a muted server, e.g. <@&123456789012345678>.
# DISCORD_RED_MENTION=

# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, Ollama, OpenRouter, …). The model only extracts facts
# from text the job fetched; every quote is checked against that text.
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://host:port/v1
# LLM_MODEL=qwen38
# LLM_API_KEY=
# Qwen-style models think by default and sometimes return nothing; true sends enable_thinking=false.
# LLM_DISABLE_THINKING=true

# Where the web app lives, for the links in Discord messages.
# WEB_BASE=http://localhost:3240
